      "source": [
        "## U-Net Architecture in PyTorch\n",
        "\n",
        "This section provides a basic implementation of the U-Net architecture using PyTorch. The U-Net is a convolutional neural network designed for image segmentation, particularly effective in biomedical image analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Imports and Basic Convolutional Block\n",
        "\n",
        "First, we import the necessary PyTorch modules and define a `ConvBlock` which consists of two convolutional layers, each followed by Batch Normalization and a ReLU activation function. This block is a fundamental component used throughout the U-Net."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ebe7043c"
      },
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "import torch.nn as nn\n",
        "import torch.nn.functional as F\n",
        "\n",
        "class ConvBlock(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels, out_channels):\n",
        "        super(ConvBlock, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.block = nn.Sequential(\n",
        "            nn.Conv2d(in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=3, padding=1),\n",
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(out_channels),\n",
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),\n",
        "            nn.Conv2d(out_channels, out_channels, kernel_size=3, padding=1),\n",
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(out_channels),\n",
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        return self.block(x)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c52b5b1d"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 2. Encoder (Downsampling Path)\n",
        "\n",
        "The encoder path (or contracting path) of the U-Net reduces the spatial dimensions of the input image while increasing the feature channels. It typically consists of repeated application of the convolutional block followed by a max-pooling operation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "33fdecbc"
      },
      "source": [
        "class Encoder(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels, out_channels):\n",
        "        super(Encoder, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.conv = ConvBlock(in_channels, out_channels)\n",
        "        self.pool = nn.MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        skip_connection = self.conv(x)\n",
        "        output = self.pool(skip_connection)\n",
        "        return output, skip_connection"
      ],
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9b0fbac1"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 3. Decoder (Upsampling Path)\n",
        "\n",
        "The decoder path (or expansive path) aims to recover the spatial information and combine it with the high-resolution features from the encoder via skip connections. It uses transposed convolutions (or upsampling followed by convolution) to increase spatial dimensions and then applies convolutional blocks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d7618184"
      },
      "source": [
        "class Decoder(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels, out_channels):\n",
        "        super(Decoder, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.upconv = nn.ConvTranspose2d(in_channels, in_channels // 2, kernel_size=2, stride=2)\n",
        "        self.conv = ConvBlock(in_channels, out_channels)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x, skip_connection):\n",
        "        x = self.upconv(x)\n",
        "        # Pad or crop if dimensions don't match exactly due to pooling/upconv\n",
        "        diffY = skip_connection.size()[2] - x.size()[2]\n",
        "        diffX = skip_connection.size()[3] - x.size()[3]\n",
        "        x = F.pad(x, [diffX // 2, diffX - diffX // 2,\n",
        "                        diffY // 2, diffY - diffY // 2])\n",
        "\n",
        "        x = torch.cat((skip_connection, x), dim=1)\n",
        "        x = self.conv(x)\n",
        "        return x"
      ],
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "63a8f4e4"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 4. U-Net Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, we assemble the full U-Net model by combining the encoder and decoder paths. The model takes an input image and outputs a segmentation map with the same spatial dimensions but with a specified number of classes (output channels)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "37ae957d"
      },
      "source": [
        "class UNet(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels=1, out_channels=1, features=[64, 128, 256, 512]):\n",
        "        super(UNet, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.encoders = nn.ModuleList()\n",
        "        self.decoders = nn.ModuleList()\n",
        "        self.bottleneck = ConvBlock(features[-1], features[-1] * 2)\n",
        "        self\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Encoder path\n",
        "        for feature in features:\n",
        "            self.encoders.append(Encoder(in_channels, feature))\n",
        "            in_channels = feature\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Decoder path\n",
        "        for feature in reversed(features):\n",
        "            self.decoders.append(Decoder(feature * 2, feature))\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.final_conv = nn.Conv2d(features[0], out_channels, kernel_size=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        skip_connections = []\n",
        "        for encoder in self.encoders:\n",
        "            x, skip = encoder(x)\n",
        "            skip_connections.append(skip)\n",
        "\n",
        "        x = self.bottleneck(x)\n",
        "        skip_connections = skip_connections[::-1] # Reverse for proper concatenation\n",
        "\n",
        "        for i, decoder in enumerate(self.decoders):\n",
        "            x = decoder(x, skip_connections[i])\n",
        "\n",
        "        return self.final_conv(x)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": []
    },
